## ⚠️ Global Constraint 1 — this plan intentionally does NOT mirror `ruby/12_context`'s file layout

`ruby/12_context` is not built on steps 10–11's MCP-host architecture,
despite `ITERATIONS.md` claiming it is (verified false against the actual
source — see below). It has no `mcp/` directory, no `tasks/` directory,
and reverts to `tools/mud.rb`/`tools/file_system.rb`/`tools/shell.rb` —
the pre-MCP direct-tool-registration model step 10's own README says was
"deleted and replaced." `tasks/` (`Tasks::Base`/`Tasks::Player`) existed
in every step 00–11 and is simply gone in 12.

A first version of this plan treated that as ground truth to port
faithfully (matching this project's usual "port Ruby's drift, not its
prose" rule). **That direction has been superseded**: this revision
instead keeps Python's existing MCP-host + `Tasks` architecture intact
and layers only step 12's real, new features on top — explicitly directed
this session, trading "byte-for-byte architectural fidelity to one
drifted Ruby snapshot" for "cumulative capability across the whole port."
Concretely, this plan **does not**:

- delete `python/src/boukensha/tasks/` or `mcp/`
- delete `python/src/boukensha/tools/mcp.py`
- add `tools/mud.py`, `tools/file_system.py`, `tools/shell.py`
- add a `mud_manager` sibling package (Ruby's `MudManager::Session`/
  `Primitives` port, ~686 lines, is not needed — MUD access stays MCP-based)
- remove `Config.tasks()`/`Config.mcp_servers`/`Config.user_prompts_dir`/
  `Config.PROMPTS_DIR`, or `Registry.registered()` (still used by
  `tools/mcp.py`)

**Direct payoff of this choice:** unlike the faithful-port draft (which
would have broken every prior step's `example.py` — see that draft's own
Confirmed Decision 1 for the cost analysis), **this plan's regression
check should come back clean across steps 00–11**, since no existing API
surface is removed, only added to. That's Task 16's explicit final check.

**Cost of this choice, stated plainly:** `python/12_context`'s tools stay
MCP-based (matching 10–11) while `ruby/12_context`'s tools are direct
in-process registration. The two languages' step-12 folders are no longer
structurally parallel the way steps 00–11 were — a deliberate, documented
fork, not an oversight. Flag this in `IMPLEMENTATION.md` (Task 17) so a
future step that tries to diff `ruby/13_*` against `ruby/12_context`
doesn't get confused about why Python's lineage looks different.

